## Task 5 - Operators & Redirection

### Operators

| Operator | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `&` | Run command in background |
| `&&` | Run second command after first succeeds |
| `>` | Redirect output (overwrite file) |
| `>>` | Redirect output (append to file) |

### Examples

Overwrite a file

```bash
echo "TryHackMe" > thm
```

Append to a file

```bash
echo "thm" >> thm
```

View file

```bash
cat thm
```

Run two commands

```bash
mkdir test && cd test
```

Background execution

```bash
sleep 30 &
```

### Answers

**Operator that waits for the first command**

```
&&
```

**Redirector that appends without overwriting**

```
>>
```

